            <div xml:id="d384">

                <pb facs="0538" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/4356</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 426</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-05-12">May 12, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your despatch No. 3141 of
                    February 24, 1936, transmitting a copy of the note from the Dominican Government
                    containing the views of that Government with respect to the interpretation to be
                    given Article III of the American-Dominican Convention of December 27, 1924,
                    concerning the pledges of future revenues by the Dominican Government, there is
                    transmitted herewith a draft of a note which you will please address to the
                    Minister of Foreign Relations in answer to his note transmitted with your
                    despatch under acknowledgment.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner
                            Welles</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d384-a1.xml" xpointer="d384-a1"/>
            </div>
